  "problem": "$$\n∀{w}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{I}\\end{aligned}}\\in Z,\\,{w}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{II}\\end{aligned}}∣({x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{III}\\end{aligned}}+3)\n$$\n\nWhich occurrences of the variables in the expression above are free?",
  "worked_solution": "Let's examine our expression and mark the occurrences of the variables as bound $(\\text{b})$ or free $(\\text{f}).$\n\n- Occurrence I of the variable $w$ is *bound* since it's placed right next to the quantifier $∀:$\n\n$$\n∀{w}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in Z,\\,w∣(x+3)\n$$\n\n- Occurrence II of the variable $w$ is *bound* since it lies within the scope of the quantifier $∀w$ that uses $w:$\n\n$$\n∀w\\in Z,\\,\\overset{\\text{scope of }∀w}{\\overset{⏞}{{w}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}∣(x+3)}}\n$$\n\n- Occurrence III of the variable $x$ is *free* since it isn't placed right next to a quantifier and it doesn't lie within the scope of a quantifier that uses $x.$\n\nThe occurrences of variables in the expression are as follows:\n\n$$\n∀{w}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in Z,\\,{w}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}∣({x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{f}\\end{aligned}}+3)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the free occurrence is \"III only.\"",
